' Shared PlantUML style for the Supermarket Inventory Tracking System SAD.
' Included by every diagram with:  !include style.puml
'
' This file is an include, not a diagram: it carries no start directive, so the
' render script and the lint skip it. Every real diagram pulls in these settings so
' colour, font and arrow styling stay identical across authors and views.

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Serif
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
' Connector colour: a dark navy that prints solid and reads as the darkest ink on
' the page, so the connectors stand out from every (lighter) element fill and stay
' distinct in grayscale.
skinparam ArrowColor #1C3F6E
skinparam ArrowFontColor #15243B
skinparam ComponentBorderColor #203864
skinparam ComponentBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam InterfaceBorderColor #1C3F6E
skinparam InterfaceBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor #203864
skinparam QueueBorderColor #203864
skinparam NodeBorderColor #203864
skinparam RectangleBorderColor #203864
' Annotations (notes): a warm neutral fill with a brown border, so a note is a
' different ink from every coloured element and from the connectors in grayscale.
skinparam NoteBorderColor #7F6000
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFF3D6

' Shared, saturated, print-safe colour vocabulary. Use these exact fills so the same
' kind of element reads the same way in every view. The four fills were chosen so that
' they separate in grayscale as well as in colour (listed here darkest to lightest):
'   #8E7CC3  persistent store (queue / database)            gray ~ 0.54
'   #6FA8DC  external system / boundary element (blue)      gray ~ 0.62
'   #93C47D  store-side runtime element (green)             gray ~ 0.68
'   #F1C232  distribution-center runtime element (gold)     gray ~ 0.75
' Connectors are the dark navy #1C3F6E; note annotations are the warm #FFF3D6.
